{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Inequality Symbol.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Inequality Symbol.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"inequality symbol inequality symbol","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Inequality Symbol.md","fileName":"Inequality Symbol.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Inequality Symbol","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Linear Inequalities and Intervals]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear Inequalities and Intervals","Open Endpoint","Closed Endpoint","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Inequality Symbol.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Inequality Symbol.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"inequality symbol inequality symbol","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Inequality Symbol.md","fileName":"Inequality Symbol.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Inequality Symbol","heading":"Inequality Symbol","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An inequality symbol states the ordering relationship between two quantities:\n\n- (a<b): (a) is less than (b)\n- (a>b): (a) is greater than (b)\n- (a\\leq b): (a) is less than or equal to (b)\n- (a\\geq b): (a) is greater than or equal to (b)\n\nThe strict symbols exclude equality, while the inclusive symbols permit it. On a graph, that difference is shown through an [[Open Endpoint]] or [[Closed Endpoint]]. Reversing the order of the two expressions also reverses the symbol: (a<b) is equivalent to (b>a).","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear Inequalities and Intervals","Open Endpoint","Closed Endpoint","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Inequality Symbol.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Inequality Symbol.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sour